# Flight report — mannequin, t23

**Sweep (k0–k4).** Started at (0, 0, 1.5) facing −180°, looking at a blank wall. Turned left in four 45° steps: −137° (wall corner, pillar), −94° (glassed bay with desks), −49° (long glass-partitioned bay, stool), and at **−8° a gate appeared** — two yellow posts with teal, about 25° left of the tick. That was the only opening I saw; the other three quadrants were wall or glazed bays, so I stopped sweeping.

**Commit (k4–k7).** Committed to the gate at room bearing ≈ **+17°**, since it led toward the unseen +x end of the room. Closed 1.4 m (k4), squared up with a pure 12° left turn to put the gap on the tick (k5), then flew straight through at σ 0.5 (k6). By k7 the posts had split to the frame edges and the teal bar showed in the downward panel — a clean transit into a new bay.

**First sighting.** **k7**, at (2.60, 0.14), heading +9°: a standing figure about a quarter of the panel tall behind a long tan table. I called it left of the tick in that decision — that was wrong, and I corrected it at k8: it was on the **R** side, ~18° right. Once close (k10–k13) it was unmistakably the mannequin: grey head, dark top, dark trousers, pale bare feet, and completely motionless across six consecutive views.

**Estimated mannequin position:** about **x 7.9, y −0.5**, standing on/behind the tan platform.

**Final pose:** x 7.06, y −0.28, z 1.56, heading −11°.

**Did I end in front of it?** Yes. It filled the forward panel head to feet, sitting just inside the 10° dead band right of the centre tick, at roughly 0.85–1.0 m — I held zero movement for the last three decisions rather than making a third small right-turn correction, which R4 forbids. The one blemish is that residual ~10° bearing offset: I'm a touch off its centreline rather than dead square on it.
